# Derivation of the First DCM Identity

Goal: show that

\[
C_i^{\,B}\,\dot C_B^{\,i} = [\omega]^\times
\]

where the “cross-product matrix” \( [\omega]^\times \) is defined by

\[
[\omega]^\times \mathbf x := \boldsymbol\omega \times \mathbf x
\]

---

## Step 1: Start from DCM orthogonality

Because \(C_B^{\,i}\) is a direction cosine matrix (a rotation matrix), it is orthogonal:

\[
C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T = I
\]

---

## Step 2: Differentiate the orthogonality condition

Differentiate both sides with respect to time:

\[
\frac{d}{dt}\left(C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T\right) = \frac{d}{dt}(I) = 0
\]

Apply the product rule:

\[
\dot C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T + C_B^{\,i}(\dot C_B^{\,i})^T = 0
\]

---

## Step 3: Rearrange and identify skew-symmetry

Rearrange:

\[
\dot C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T = -\,C_B^{\,i}(\dot C_B^{\,i})^T
\]

Now use the transpose rule \( (AB)^T = B^T A^T \):

\[
\left(\dot C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T\right)^T
=
C_B^{\,i}(\dot C_B^{\,i})^T
\]

Substitute this into the rearranged equation:

\[
\dot C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T
=
-\left(\dot C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T\right)^T
\]

Define

\[
A := \dot C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T
\]

Then the previous line reads

\[
A = -A^T
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
A^T = -A
\]

By definition, \(A^T=-A\) means \(A\) is **skew-symmetric**.

---

## Step 4: Any \(3\times 3\) skew-symmetric matrix equals a cross-product matrix

A general \(3\times 3\) skew-symmetric matrix has the form

\[
A =
\begin{bmatrix}
0 & -\omega_z & \omega_y \\
\omega_z & 0 & -\omega_x \\
-\omega_y & \omega_x & 0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

for some vector \(\boldsymbol\omega = (\omega_x,\omega_y,\omega_z)^T\).  
This matrix is exactly \( [\omega]^\times \). Therefore there exists a unique \(\boldsymbol\omega\) such that

\[
\dot C_B^{\,i}(C_B^{\,i})^T = [\omega]^\times
\]

---

## Step 5: Convert to the standard form \(C_i^{\,B}\dot C_B^{\,i}\)

Since \(C_i^{\,B} = (C_B^{\,i})^T\), the identity becomes

\[
C_i^{\,B}\dot C_B^{\,i} = [\omega]^\times
\]

---

## Final Result

\[
\boxed{
C_i^{\,B}\,\dot C_B^{\,i} = [\omega]^\times
}
\]